====Adverb====
{{en-adv|further}}

# {{lb|en|not comparable}} To or in a [[previous]] condition or place.
#: {{ux|en|He gave '''back''' the money.}}
#: {{ux|en|I left my mobile phone '''back''' at the hotel. I’ll have to go '''back''' and get it.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=2|passage=We drove '''back''' to the office with some concern on my part at the prospect of so large a case. Sunning himself on the board steps, I saw for the first time Mr. Farquhar Fenelon Cooke. He was dressed out in broad gaiters and bright tweeds, like an English tourist, and his face might have belonged to Dagon, idol of the Philistines.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=52| title=The new masters and commanders|url=http://www.economist.com/news/international/21579039-chinas-growing-empire-ports-abroad-mainly-about-trade-not-aggression-new-masters| passage=From the ground, Colombo’s port does not look like much. Those entering it are greeted by wire fences, walls dating '''back''' to colonial times and security posts. For mariners leaving the port after lonely nights on the high seas, the delights of the B52 Night Club and Stallion Pub lie a stumble away.}}
# In a direction opposite to that in which someone or something is facing or normally pointing.
#: {{ux|en|Someone pushed me in the chest and I fell '''back'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The grandfather clock toppled '''back''' and crashed to the ground.}}
#: {{ux|en|Her arm was bent '''back''' at an odd angle.}}
# In a direction opposite to the usual or desired direction of movement or progress, physically or figuratively.
#: {{ux|en|Wind the film '''back''' a few frames.}}
#: {{ux|en|Don’t forget to put the clocks '''back''' by one hour tonight!}}
#: {{ux|en|This mishap has set the project '''back''' considerably.}}
# Towards, into or in the past.
#: {{ux|en|These records go '''back''' years.}}
#: {{ux|en|He built a time machine and travelled '''back''' to 1800.}}
#: {{ux|en|Think '''back''' to how you felt last year.}}
#: {{ux|en|Everything was simpler '''back''' in the old days.}}
# Away from someone or something; at a distance.
#: {{ux|en|Keep '''back'''! It could explode at any moment!}}
# Away from the front or from an edge (of something or someone).
#: {{ux|en|Sit all the way '''back''' in your chair.}}
#: {{ux|en|Step '''back''' from the curb.}} <!-- Step further back-->
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage=Pretty soon I struck into a sort of path{{nb...}}. It twisted and turned,{{...}}and opened out into a big clear space like a lawn. And, '''back''' of the lawn, was a big, old-fashioned house, with piazzas stretching in front of it, and all blazing with lights. 'Twas the house I'd seen the roof of from the beach.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1923|author=J. Allan Dunn|title=Wild Justice|journal=Adventure|volume=39|page=75
|passage='''Back''' of the man, straightening himself while the withdrawing water swirled about his ankles, mounted the next incoming wave.}}
# So as to shrink, recede or move aside, or cause to do so.
#: {{ux|en|This tree is dying '''back'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Clear '''back''' all this vegetation.}}
#: {{ux|en|Draw '''back''' the curtains and let in some light.}}
# In a manner that [[impede]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Fear held him '''back'''.}}
# {{lb|en|not comparable}} In a [[reciprocal]] manner; [[in return]].
#: {{ux|en|If you hurt me, I’ll hurt you '''back'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The light bounces '''back''' off the mirror.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:National Geographic|year=1989|month=May|volume=175|number=5|title=The Baltic: Arena of Power|author=Priit J. Vesilind|page=604
|text="How is it, comrades?" the admiral shouted through a bullhorn at each ship. "Rah, rah, rah!" the sailors shouted '''back''' in unison.}}
#* {{quote-av
|en
|url=https://ia800705.us.archive.org/33/items/Penn_Radio_archive/The.Penn.Jillette.Radio.Show.2006.05.09.mp3
